hey all it's kevin van oort here with  some quick impressions of the time I've  spent over the last few days playing  total war Attila which is due out in  February 2015 a little over a month from  now I was sad that the preview version  didn't let me play as the Huns but I did  want to get a taste of nomadic life and  so I chose another migratory group the  Ostrogoths and as it turns out life as  an austere goth is pretty dangerous  I began as a homeless horde but I chose  to settle quickly into an abandoned  settlement and sent my to pre-existing  armies out to conquer such settlements  aren't blessed with full fertility so I  knew that I wouldn't be filling my food  stores as quickly as I like I figured my  fledgling village might provide some  sustenance for the years to come but man  I was wrong the Hun's were having none  of it my visions of exploiting the new  Total War options of plundering and  pillaging were crushed I had to abandon  my dreams though I did come to  appreciate the ability to drop camp  anywhere and make a home for my  traveling horde it was as the sassanid  empire that I was able to explore some  of the games newer additions in greater  detail one of those additions is the  political system that governs factional  power struggles welcome worthy guests I  trust you bring words that will enhance  the honor of your people in our eyes the  goal is to maintain your ruling families  power and avoid the interference of  nobles that seek to usurp it for  instance you can assassinate nobles that  are giving you trouble or buy their  favor for me I found success in  assigning governorships to the grandees  and finding wives for my generals this  is all very simple to accomplish once  you grow accustomed to total war till as  busy interface understanding exactly how  these options affect your progress and  potency doesn't come as easily I have a  handle on the basics at this point but I  don't yet feel like the mastermind of a  grand political plan I can certainly  March with the best of them however in  one of my city's unrest broke out after  I failed to maintain public order and  thus the first sassanids civil war began  and the first battle that I had a chance  of emerging victorious ensued  fortunately I'd kept my armies healthy  and well equipped in spite of my  decisions to choose mostly civil  technology at a good array of troops as  well as three deployables of fire pit  and two sets of steaks which you can  place on the ground as defensive  measures  the prototypical total war battle ensued  featuring over a thousand men locked in  heated skirmishes the  rock-paper-scissors relationships  between units are easy to understand  it's good positioning and battlefield  management that wins battles well that  ends a bit of AI exploitation the  preview version of total war Attila  features many of the same hey I troubles  the previous games held along with the  usual performance struggles here's  hoping they're ironed out before full  release it goes without saying that i  was still invested turn-by-turn in the  future of my Empire not really a  surprise in a series known for absorbing  players for weeks months and years I  wish your own empires all the best for  when the game is fully released on  februari 17  you
 

